From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The options in the lower menu's panel (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With the lower menu on and the Pokétch up, OPTIONS ends the Pokétch
behind the panel's black and draws an options page on the sub engine,
tall, in tabs: SETTINGS (the game's six, 60 FPS, SMOOTH 3D, START WITH),
ENHANCEMENTS and CHEATS (with GIVE ITEMS on a page of its own). The page
is drawn off the screen as one picture and cut into tiles; touches come
from the port's panel buttons. The game's settings go in its save as its
options screen sets them; the port's in the port's own file. Closed, the
Pokétch comes back; another menu button pressed on the page is acted on
after (the bag, the party, the trainer case and the save straight on from
the black panel). OPTIONS in the bag, the party or the trainer case goes
to the page behind the black, as SAVE. START WITH chooses the panel's tab
when the game starts. Without the menu it's the DS's options screen.
The page opens again on the tab and cards it closed on; the FRAME card is
drawn as a message box in the frame chosen.

The enhancements and cheats (port_options.h: the port's settings):
EXP ON CATCH (the catch stops after "Gotcha!" while the script pays out
experience as for a defeated Pokémon), PARTY EXP SHARE (every Pokémon
able to: the participants their share, the others half), TRADE EVO AT 40
(a trade evolution by level 40), HMs WITHOUT MOVES (a field move whose HM
the bag has is the party's first Pokémon's: the scripts' checks and the
party menu's Fly, Defog and Flash), AUTO-RUN (running unless B is held,
with the running shoes), ALWAYS CATCH, INSTANT VICTORY (the player's
attacks knock out), FAST EGGS, INFINITE MONEY, WILD ENCOUNTERS (off,
1/4, 1/2, 2x) and SHINY ODDS (to always).

On the wider screen: the Pokédex's page after a catch laid out as the
info page (its maps came round beside the DS's screen), and the cry
page's wave from edge to edge (a window of its own, 512 wide, shown on
beside the DS's screen) with its band's lower edge at the screen's bottom.
